post.description:
Settle an approval condition — a factual entry, OPEN → MET, no dual control (PRD1042-1937).

Front office and back office settle. A non-open condition (already met/waived/expired) is a 409;
an unknown condition, or a cross-tenant / unknown financing, is 404.

Confirm a draft/pending-confirmation partner — single-actor FO action per
US 13.5 (Sys Admin ✓, FO ✓, BO/Risk ✗). No Four-Eyes approval (PRD1042-1449);
risk-sensitive roles are governed separately via partner_role_assign.

get.description:
PRD1042-1894 Block 10 — the auditor (and Bank Admin) exports the full change log as CSV.

No version history in the MVP → this append-only log is the history. BPU + Support + Auditor;
others/cross-tenant → 404. The export access is itself audited (WTC_AUDIT_TRAIL_EXPORTED).

DocumentRowRead.description:
One row of the table: File · Type · Owner · Source · Date. The file downloads from ``/media/{document_id}``.
``removable`` — the table may remove it (``entry_id`` is what the owner's remove route takes);
``managed_on`` — shown here, edited elsewhere (``collateral_card``: the DAT total card on the Collaterals tab).

PaymentMode.description:
When in each period the instalment falls due (PRD1042-2269) — MILK ``Zahlmodus``.

Captured only. The refinancing calculation stays arrears-only (PO item 7a) whatever this says;
the field records the lease being refinanced, it does not configure the bank's cash flow.
